# The directory that CONTAINS your Dark Souls Remastered install — not the install itself.
#
# `cargo xtask` scans every immediate subdirectory for a DarkSoulsRemastered.exe and
# runs the AOB scans against each one it finds, emitting one set of base addresses per
# game version. That is why it wants the parent: it needs something to iterate over.
#
#   steamapps/common/            <- point DSR_INSTALLS_DIR here
#   |-- DARK SOULS REMASTERED/   <- scanned, version detected from the PE resource
#   |   `-- DarkSoulsRemastered.exe
#   |-- DARK SOULS III/          <- no DSR exe, skipped
#   `-- ...
#
# Use SINGLE quotes. dotenv processes backslash escapes inside double quotes, so
# `KEY="D:\SteamLibrary\..."` fails to parse and leaves the variable unset. `cargo xtask`
# warns when it had to skip a malformed .env.
#
# Steam default:
#   DSR_INSTALLS_DIR='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common'
# Secondary drive:
#   DSR_INSTALLS_DIR='D:\SteamLibrary\steamapps\common'
DSR_INSTALLS_DIR='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common'
